Z||000000||phillip||05-09-2000||02:24 AM||||<BR>sent an e-mail to sport compact car mag. to correct them where they mentioned fieros in the mr2 artical (june 2000). took the opportunity to suggest a fiero artical and/or build up. recieved an e-mail back saying they'd consider it. could have been humoring me but maybe a few more e-mails might make it a more worthwhile idea.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.sportcompactcarweb.com" TARGET=_blank>www.sportcompactcarweb.com</A> <P>can't hurt to try.||||reg||1
Z||000001||phillip||05-10-2000||02:07 AM||||<BR>you're not interested?||||reg||1
Z||000002||loafer87gt||05-10-2000||02:25 AM||||The guys at SCC are pretty openminded. I wrote them a couple of years ago and asked why they never featured any buildups of Fieros, and their answer was pretty straightforward. They said that they would love to have a modified Fiero in their mag, but no one has came forward to offer to show their car in the mag!!! They said thats the way they setup their mag, they don't go out seeking out owners, its all based on owners coming to them willing to show their car in the mag. I would love to see someone with a DOHC 3.4 or Northstar with coil over suspension and all the other goodies write them and offer their car. I think it would be a good wakeup call to the ricers out their who think that the Fiero has no aftermarket potential. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||phillip||05-10-2000||10:53 AM||||but along with feature cars they also do project cars, and not always new ones. i know they did an early '80s carolla a while back. also a 1st gen crx, 1st gen rx7 and 1st gen mr2. all fairly recent or in the last year or two. not always full on projects. some times just wheel tire upgrades or just engine work.              they have no reason to consider it if no one shows any interest.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||05-10-2000||12:36 PM||||Over 10 years ago Fieros West was in an early issue of SCC. About 4 years ago I sent them 2 articles about 2 of our best Fieros on the basis that they would schedule a photo shoot for them...still waiting....<P>They are so knee deep into the imports, and just now touching on the domestics, I almost wonder how our Fieros would fit in their world aside from a nice little "Blast from the Past" ditty.||||reg||1
